--- !u!114 &1059882258
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1059882255}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d0b4d18b988aef64fbfa0c5751ecf77d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  description: 'The LextingInputModuleManager enables you to choose your target platform.
    For each platform, the Lexting interface will throw errors if you don''t assign
    references to your controller.


    For example, in QUEST_HANDS mode, you need
    to drag the head, left hand, and right hand of your Oculus rig into the fields
    above.


    All Quest and OpenXR platforms require head, left hand, and right
    hand references.


    All Leap platforms require just left hand and right hand.


    NOTE:
    If you assign controller references in one mode, the assignment doesn''t carry
    across to other modes since there are times when you won''t want one to overwrite
    the other. If you are using a single controller to deploy to multiple platforms,
    you will need to assign it to each mode individually.'
